{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bearer token bearer token","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md","fileName":"Bearer Token.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bearer Token","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bearer token bearer token","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md","fileName":"Bearer Token.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bearer Token","heading":"Bearer Token","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A bearer token authorizes whoever presents it, so possession of the token is sufficient for the protected server to consider the associated access claim. The stock-checker client places its token in the HTTP authorization header before calling the API.\n\nBecause the credential is usable by its bearer, it must be protected in transport and storage and limited to the intended resource and scope. The API validates it before the controller's protected operation is allowed to run.","tags":["baby"],"links":["OAuth 2.0 and IdentityServer","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"bearer token bearer token","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Bearer Token.md","fileName":"Bearer Token.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Bearer Token","hea